  "verified": [
    "Mixed historical source pins, changed parent types, exact decimal conversion, required attribute defaults, active owner repair and source-version state mapping commit together; descendant definitions and bindings remain pinned.",
    "Stale plans, states, cohorts and owner activity, hidden bindings, foreign owners, foreign receipts, revoked authority and inaccessible idempotency replays fail closed.",
    "A late production journal failure rolls back heads, definitions, pins, values, owner/state, revisions, base/typed/normalized receipts, audit, outbox and idempotency success. The same key retries to exactly one receipt.",
    "Immutable receipt tuples and hashes match actual before/after revision snapshots. SQL rejects missing companions, forged tuples, malformed nested policy plans, mismatched source/target references and normalized-row mutations.",
    "Real HTTP preview/execution/read-back enforce CSRF, If-Match, digest consent and idempotency. Legacy receipt routes reject incomplete attribute-only presentation of typed migrations.",
    "An empty cohort still binds the current authored head resolution and records a zero-asset immutable receipt.",
    "Disposable concurrency cases prove both revocation lock orderings, explicit tenant principal scope, inactive-owner repair, rollback lock release and forged nested-trigger denial.",
    "Finite numeric boundaries and aggregate exponent expansion preserve cross-runtime hashes. Physical JSONB limits reject oversized receipts before preview or execution writes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is a bounded synchronous development qualification, not full MOD/AT-MOD/M2 acceptance or a release.",
    "Browser, accessibility and rendered UI verification are recorded separately and must not be inferred from this API report.",
    "Durable large-cohort migrations, constrained relations, other model kinds, scopes/responsibilities, glossary/reference data and later ingress enforcement remain required programme work.",
    "Transaction rollback and a disposable schema upgrade do not establish production backup/restore, released-predecessor upgrade, enterprise HA or scale.",
    "The scoped SQL canonical serializer supports contract-safe ASCII object keys and finite JavaScript JSON numbers; decimal attributes remain exact strings. It is not a general canonical JSON standard."
  ],
